# tools/a/aurora_placement_witness.rish -- can row 7 be placed?
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/a/aurora_placement_witness.rish
#
# First witness for moonshot 7 of
# `active-designing/date/20260910/20260910-060204_the-bounded-torus-moonshots.md`: Aurora as a small torus of
# cores, whose first witness the row names as a placement map -- which module sits on which node,
# and the hop count for every pair.
#
# THE ROW'S OWN FALSIFIER: "the reachable boards are mesh rather than torus, which would leave the
# wrap-around hops the map depends on unavailable." Both halves of the row are gradeable with no
# board at all, and this witness reads them separately.
#
# THE GEOMETRY. At the 4-core grid the row names FIRST, a 2 x 2 torus IS a 2 x 2 mesh: `i + 1 mod 2`
# and `i - 1 mod 2` name the same node, so each wrap link duplicates a mesh link the board already
# has. Equal diameter, equal distinct link count, equal mean pair distance -- one graph under two
# names. A mesh board therefore takes nothing away, and the row's falsifier cannot fire where the
# row starts. At 16 cores it fires with something real behind it: diameter 6 to 4, mean distance
# 2.6667 to 2.1333, a fifth of the average hop bought by 8 extra links.
#
# THE OPERAND. A placement map minimizes `sum over pairs of w(i,j) x hops(i,j)`, so it wants a
# module-to-module communication WEIGHT. This tree holds STRUCTURE instead: cross-room dependency
# resolved through the import symlinks it files by hand, one edge per importing source file, a
# startup read and a hot loop indistinguishable. The measurement sits in the scan's own keys.
#
# WHAT THIS WITNESS DOES NOT REACH. Whether a 16-core torus board becomes reachable, and whether a
# weight gathered later would place these rooms well. It proves the row's first grid cannot
# falsify, and that the operand its first witness needs is not in the tree today.

say "aurora-placement: Style Gauge, Meter -- two halves of one row, graded apart."
say "aurora-placement: Lens TAME -- a falsifier that cannot fire is a sentence rather than a test."

# --- The reading -------------------------------------------------------------
say "aurora-placement: reading the geometry and the operand..."
let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/a/aurora_placement_scan.sh"]
say scan.out
assert scan.ok else "aurora-placement: the scan refused -- read its own keys"
assert scan.out contains "verdict=read" else "aurora-placement: the scan reached no verdict"

# invariant: the reading names the row and the page it grades, so a key pasted out of context
# still says which sentence it is about.
assert scan.out contains "row=7" else "aurora-placement: the reading named no row"
assert scan.out contains "the-bounded-torus-moonshots.md" else "aurora-placement: the reading named no page"

# invariant: at the 4-core grid the two topologies are one graph, so the row's falsifier has
# nothing to take away there.
assert scan.out contains "four_core_same_graph=yes" else "aurora-placement: the 2x2 torus and mesh parted"
assert scan.out contains "four_core_falsifier_can_fire=no" else "aurora-placement: the 4-core falsifier was read as live"

# invariant: at 16 cores the wrap buys a real cut, so the row is worth keeping rather than dropping.
assert scan.out contains "sixteen_core_falsifier_can_fire=yes" else "aurora-placement: the 16-core falsifier was read as silent"
assert scan.out contains "sixteen_core_diameter_cut=2" else "aurora-placement: the 16-core diameter cut moved"
assert scan.out contains "sixteen_core_mean_cut_share=0.2000" else "aurora-placement: the 16-core mean cut moved"

# invariant: the mesh diameter at 16 cores is the closed form 2(k-1) and the torus 2*floor(k/2),
# stated here so a reader checks the arithmetic rather than the program.
assert scan.out contains "torus_diameter=4 mesh_diameter=6" else "aurora-placement: the 16-core diameters left their closed forms"

# invariant: the operand reading opened the tree at all -- a room census of zero would make every
# later key read clean while measuring nothing.
assert scan.out contains "rooms=" else "aurora-placement: no room census was taken"
assert scan.out contains "room_pairs=" else "aurora-placement: no room graph was read"
assert scan.out contains "loom_keys=" else "aurora-placement: the journal was not read for a weight"

# invariant: 44 rooms do not sit on 4 nodes one apiece, so the map the row proposes needs a
# coarsening its sentence never states.
assert scan.out contains "coarsening_needed k=2 nodes=4" else "aurora-placement: the 4-node coarsening went unread"
assert scan.out contains "coarsening_needed k=4 nodes=16" else "aurora-placement: the 16-node coarsening went unread"

# --- The bounds --------------------------------------------------------------
# invariant: every collection this scan builds names its maximum, so a tree that grows past one is
# refused at the edge rather than read short in silence.
assert scan.out contains "max_grids=" else "aurora-placement: the grid bound is unnamed"
assert scan.out contains "max_rooms=" else "aurora-placement: the room bound is unnamed"
assert scan.out contains "max_imports=" else "aurora-placement: the import bound is unnamed"
assert scan.out contains "max_keys=" else "aurora-placement: the key bound is unnamed"
assert scan.out contains "rooms_over_bound=no" else "aurora-placement: the room census stands over its bound"
assert scan.out contains "grids_over_bound=0" else "aurora-placement: a grid was dropped at the bound"

# --- The capacity term, and the unit it refuses ------------------------------
# invariant: a node holds a bounded amount of code, so a map from rooms to nodes is feasible only
# if no room is larger than a node -- a term this tree DOES hold, where the traffic term is absent.
assert scan.out contains "room_bytes_total=" else "aurora-placement: no capacity term was read"
assert scan.out contains "largest_room_share=" else "aurora-placement: the largest room's share went unread"
assert scan.out contains "room_bytes_over_bound=no" else "aurora-placement: the byte census stands over its bound"

# invariant: one room is forty percent of this tree's Rye, so no assignment of MODULES to nodes
# exists at either grid the row names, and the unit of the row's first witness is what must change.
assert scan.out contains "capacity k=4 nodes=16" else "aurora-placement: the 16-node capacity went unread"
assert scan.out contains "room_granularity=infeasible file_granularity=feasible" else "aurora-placement: the granularity verdict moved -- read the scan, then read the paper"

# --- What the proxy buys, and how wrong it may be ----------------------------
# invariant: the placement is compared against a SIZE-MATCHED baseline. A node holding many rooms
# pays nothing for the traffic inside it, so a layout free to pile rooms up beats a spread baseline
# under any weights at all -- a reading of occupancy wearing a reading of coupling.
assert scan.out contains "reading4=read" else "aurora-placement: the placement reading reached no verdict"
assert scan.out contains "matched_gain_share=" else "aurora-placement: the size-matched baseline went unread"
assert scan.out contains "busiest_node_rooms=" else "aurora-placement: the occupancy profile went unread"

# invariant: the two ways a proxy can be wrong answer oppositely, and that is the finding. Scaling
# every weight by up to 256 costs the layout nothing; moving its edges costs it everything.
assert scan.out contains "scale_drift_bites=no" else "aurora-placement: mis-scaling the weights began to cost the layout -- the finding has moved"
assert scan.out contains "structure_drift_bites=yes" else "aurora-placement: moving the edges stopped costing the layout -- the instrument is measuring occupancy again"
assert scan.out contains "proxy_survives_structure_drift_upto_pct=" else "aurora-placement: the tolerance went unread"
assert scan.out contains "proxy_keep_share=" else "aurora-placement: the keep threshold is unnamed"

# --- The control: 75 behaviors, six mutations, three pens -------------------
say "aurora-placement: the control -- a real repository in a throwaway pen..."
let ctl = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/a/aurora_placement_control.sh"]
say ctl.out
assert ctl.ok else "aurora-placement: the control refused -- read its own leg lines"
assert ctl.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "aurora-placement: the control reached no ok verdict"
assert ctl.out contains "failures=0" else "aurora-placement: a planted behavior differed from what was stated"

# invariant: the control tallies its own legs and this witness asserts the count, so a leg written
# tomorrow is heard the day it lands rather than passing unread under a green verdict.
assert ctl.out contains "legs=75" else "aurora-placement: the control's leg count moved -- read it, then raise this line"

# invariant: each of the four mutations was planted AND bit. A refusal proven only in the passing
# direction cannot be told from a bypass.
assert ctl.out contains "leg m1_bites ok" else "aurora-placement: removing the wrap-duplicate collapse went unfelt"
assert ctl.out contains "leg m2_bites ok" else "aurora-placement: replacing cyclic distance with plain distance went unfelt"
assert ctl.out contains "leg m3_bites ok" else "aurora-placement: leaving import symlinks unfollowed went unfelt"
assert ctl.out contains "leg m4_bites ok" else "aurora-placement: dropping the self-edge guard went unfelt"

# invariant: a placement needs more rooms than nodes, so the second pen carries six rooms and five
# weighted pairs whose right answer is computable by hand -- two merges, three rooms on the busiest
# node, and a cost of exactly 3 on a 2 x 2 torus.
assert ctl.out contains "leg pen2_torus_cost_by_hand ok" else "aurora-placement: the hand-computed placement cost moved"
assert ctl.out contains "leg pen2_merges_at_four ok" else "aurora-placement: heavy-edge merging stopped merging what it should"
assert ctl.out contains "leg pen2_busiest_node ok" else "aurora-placement: the occupancy the pen expects moved"
assert ctl.out contains "leg pen2_structure_drift_bites ok" else "aurora-placement: structure drift stopped biting in the pen"
assert ctl.out contains "leg pen2_scale_drift_silent ok" else "aurora-placement: scale drift began biting in the pen"
assert ctl.out contains "leg m5_bites ok" else "aurora-placement: counting symlinks as code went unfelt"
assert ctl.out contains "leg m6_bites ok" else "aurora-placement: an unmatched baseline went unfelt"

# invariant: a third pen carries no Rye at all. An empty population fits every node trivially, so
# both granularity readings answer `unread` there and the placement refuses rather than passing.
assert ctl.out contains "leg pen3_capacity_unread ok" else "aurora-placement: an empty population read as a real fit"
assert ctl.out contains "leg pen3_reading4_refuses ok" else "aurora-placement: a graph with no edges was placed anyway"

# invariant: segment matching is proven by INPUT rather than by a mutation -- the pen carries a
# room `mand` and a key `mandate_rows`, which holds `mand` as a substring and as no segment.
assert ctl.out contains "leg pen_substring_room_refused ok" else "aurora-placement: a substring room name was counted as a named room"

say "GREEN: aurora-placement -- the 4-core falsifier stays silent, the 16-core one fires, the capacity term refuses the row's own unit, and the static graph tolerates two thirds of its edges wandering."
